{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra","id":1379759,"title":"Kurdish \"freedom fighters\" in Ashirra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-09T07:49:17-07:00","id":1379759,"title":"Kurdish \"freedom fighters\" in Ashirra","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This passage is from Camarilla sourcebook v5 (I had a look at the earlier version with Chechnya part, so if this part is edited please let me know!):<br /> <br /> &quot;thinking the ashirra is a single thing, a single culture, is a prejudiced idea that will get you killed in the courts of the future. consider this: among our new allies we find saudi princes dining on the blood of women stoned to death for infidelity, a liberal \u0131t-millionnaire from jordan, turkish nationalists dreaming of the ottoman empire, kurdish freedom fighters and persian nobles longing for the glorious days of disco in 1970\u2019s teheran. they are all ashirra. they all believe in allah\u2019s pillars. yet none of them think and act in the same way.&quot;<br /> <br /> To my knowledge, freedom fighter is a relativistic term and usually, it is said if a person is sympathetic and supportive towards the goals of the so-called freedom fighter. While all other examples are more or less neutral (like Persian noble, Ottoman wannabe Turkish nationalist, and Saudi princes that drink stoned women\u2019s blood), why a Brujah (Albertzen) who chose to remain inside Camarilla, would be picking sides in a mortal conflict by calling them freedom fighters? You know how the saying goes: Someone\u2019s terrorist is another\u2019s freedom fighter (in this case the other way around).<br /> <br /> Kurdish freedom fighters who are referred here, if you consider the timing of the release of the book and the emphasis on Syrian Civil War in some other parts, are the YPG that </span></span>shares an intellectual lineage and certain overlaps in memberships and militant recruitments with the PKK, which is designated as a terrorist organization by EU and USA (if you have any other ideas that who might be those 'freedom fighters' please share your thoughts!)<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">.</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> I mean, of course, kindred manipulate and take sides on kine conflicts to their own ends and goals but I just can't imagine a supposedly neutral Cam brujah would sympathize with them. I don't think anybody in WW would intentionally promote violence but honestly, it just seems like some shitty propaganda between the lines. What do you think? Personally I really hate words like &quot;freedom fighter&quot; that, in a way, glorifies the violence. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26081-malkav19","user":"malkav19","date":". 04-09-2020, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26081-malkav19","name":"malkav19","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T09:47:54-07:00","id":1379784,"title":"","content":"Just remember the Mujahideen in Afghanistan were once referred to as freedom Fighters when it suited the United States interests. Now they are called Al Qaeda","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:02:10-07:00","id":1379787,"title":"","content":"What is the neutral term for \u201cpeople fighting to resist their own ethnic extermination\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:19:54-07:00","id":1379795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1379784#post1379784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just remember the Mujahideen in Afghanistan were once referred to as freedom Fighters when it suited the United States interests. Now they are called Al Qaeda</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This would actually make sense but a bit clearer indication or giving voice to some counter-arguments could have been better for me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1379787#post1379787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the neutral term for \u201cpeople fighting to resist their own ethnic extermination\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that is your opinion. Personally, I wouldn\u2019t name armed groups who attack and kill civilians \u201cfreedom fighters\u201d. I bet there are many people who see ISIS as legit and even as some freedom fighters just like Reagen did with the Mujahideen. In any case, terms like terrorist or freedom fighter are relative and mostly political. The neutral term could be Kurdish fighters, militia, militants and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26081-malkav19","name":"malkav19","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:23:41-07:00","id":1379796,"title":"","content":"I'll just ask:<br /> <br /> Wasn't the US supporting up until recently kurdish groups in Syria? Groups that were the frontline against Daesh and managed the prisons they were kept in? That established a democratic, egalitarian system in the areas of Syria they held from Abbas' regime? What would be the neutral term for those groups? Could the book refer to them?<br /> <br /> And then move on from this inherently politically worded thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:44:37-07:00","id":1379805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malkav19</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra#post1379759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While all other examples are more or less neutral (like Persian noble...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might need to consider what's neutral and what's not from the perspective of people on the ground, not just people a continent away. Calling someone a Persian noble that's longing for the 70s? That's an incredibly loaded thing to do by Middle Eastern standards. It might not touch on the same geopolitical issues with the concepts of violence by the citizenry, but I'd wager considerably that your average Iranian has stronger feelings about the Iranian/Persian naming conventions and how the West missuses the terms, than they do about how English speakers juggle the semantics of freedom fighters vs. terrorist. There's a reason they're called the Revolutionary Guard in Iran rather than worrying about what name best appeals to non-Farsi speakers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...why a Brujah (Albertzen) who chose to remain inside Camarilla, would be picking sides in a mortal conflict by calling them freedom fighters? </div> </div> </div>We don't really know enough about Albertzen to gauge his specific reasoning on anything. It's not like he's a long standing character in the game with lots of lore to unpack his thought processes with.<br /> <br /> Though I don't see the stretch for a Brujah to be supportive of the Kurds; even the more radical and violent PKK. The Brujah, generally, like rebels standing up to power... and aren't very picky about methods. Why would a Brujah call any Kurdish group terrorists? Because the US and UN say so?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think anybody in WW would intentionally promote violence but honestly, it just seems like some shitty propaganda between the lines. </div> </div> </div>I think you're reading way too much into this, and have demonstrated a lack of cultural knowledge of the region to get into the weeds on how a fictional character's aside about a group might be promoting anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally I really hate words like &quot;freedom fighter&quot; that, in a way, glorifies the violence. </div> </div> </div>OK. If this is actually your problem, than I don't see the point. You might not like the term, but it gets used all the time. Most people in the world accept that sometimes violence is not only necessary but a moral good; and once it moves into the moral good estimation it is inherently viewed positively. Pacifism isn't a dominant position by humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1379784#post1379784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just remember the Mujahideen in Afghanistan were once referred to as freedom Fighters when it suited the United States interests. Now they are called Al Qaeda</div> </div> </div> </div>Um.... no? Now they're called the Taliban (even if that's a gross oversimplification as well). Mujahideen is also a generic term, not a specific organization.<br /> <br /> The Afghani mujahideen didn't become Al-Qaeda. A couple of foreigners that went to Afghanistan to join the fight decided to start Al-Qaeda after the war ended to expand on the victory and use it to promote their extremist ideology by organizing all the small groups of foreign mujahideen in Afghanistan into something bigger.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T11:19:07-07:00","id":1379816,"title":"","content":"A few random factoids for the complicated political and economic elements of a RL matter in the World of Darkness:<br /> <br /> 1. The United States actually re-allied with the Kurds almost immediately after abandoning them and they remain the US' allies.<br /> <br /> 2. The Kurdish resistance in Syria are listed as a terrorist organization primarily by Russia, Assad, and Turkey due to the fact that they are interested in establishing a Kurdish state.<br /> <br /> 3. The Kurds have been allies of the USA since the US took over administration of Iraq-Kurd territory when chemical weapons were used against them.<br /> <br /> 4. It's a talking point that the Afghanistan freedom fighters against the Soviet Union (which they were) became the Taliban. The issue is a bit more complicated than that and could better be summarized as, &quot;The resistance against the Soviet Union succeeded but was then replaced by a reactionary Islamic fundamentalist state founded by their own children, many of which were raised by clerics they'd been kept with during the war. Those who resisted were killed.&quot;<br /> <br /> 5. The treatment of the Kurds as terrorists is kind of an international joke that ****ing Call of Duty made fun of as insane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/XCKsZGVIlUw\" data-code=\"XCKsZGVIlUw\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XCKsZGVIlUw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> 6. Al-Qaeda or &quot;The Foundation&quot; was founded by a Saudi Arabian group trying to get Americans out of Saudi Arabia that became a more generic anti-American one. It was given host by the Taliban and carried out attacks on the US from their soil prior to 9/11. Hence why it was justified under international law to invade them given they were receiving sanctuary and support by the Taliban.<br /> <br /> 7. This is a good argument why all commentary should be done in-universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-09-2020, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T12:29:42-07:00","id":1379831,"title":"","content":"There's also pretty big difference between talking about individual Kurdish organizations (some of whom definitely stray onto the terrorism side of things) and the Kurds as a whole. The US is allied with some Kurdish organizations, while classifying others as terrorists, because the Kurds are an ethnic group, spread over multiple countries. Which is how pretty much every nation treats non-nation actors of this sort: on a case-by-case basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:15:52-07:00","id":1379854,"title":"","content":"Right, right, sensitive territories and all, complex topic and that, but let's bring this down to vampires<br /> <br /> From Any vampires point of view, is what the OP's quoted actually appropriate? Consider this; The Ashirra doesn't cover one city that covers the entire middle east, it's in <i>different</i> cities. The Saud and the turk are going to be far, far away from eachother, just like there are few Germans in france. <br /> From an Elders perspective; Do they really care about the many, many mortal groups that are taking up arms for various ideologies? A lot of these groups have only popped up in the last century or so. It isn't just elders, it's Ancillae that predate the borders and factions of the land. <br /> <br /> To me it just reads like someone wanting to appear culturally sensitive, without actually considering that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:19:40-07:00","id":1379859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1379816#post1379816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 6. This is a good argument why all commentary should be done in-universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a rare thing I agree with you but sometimes stars align.<br /> <br /> Your Camarilla Brujah is a Camarilla Brujah. he's not checking twitter to find a political camp and cling to it's designated, proscribed formulas and ideologically correct namings.<br /> <br /> Can we just stop trying to blur in- and out-of-game universe settings please? Thanks a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:28:41-07:00","id":1379898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1379859#post1379859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a rare thing I agree with you but sometimes stars align.<br /> <br /> Your Camarilla Brujah is a Camarilla Brujah. he's not checking twitter to find a political camp and cling to it's designated, proscribed formulas and ideologically correct namings.<br /> <br /> Can we just stop trying to blur in- and out-of-game universe settings please? Thanks a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's why the disaster of a certain chapter about Chechnya was such a big one. It was originally a gay Brujah arguing with a fundamentalist Banu Haqim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:55:25-07:00","id":1379910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1379898#post1379898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's why the disaster of a certain chapter about Chechnya was such a big one. It was originally a gay Brujah arguing with a fundamentalist Banu Haqim.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You tell me. I've witnessed the shitstorm it caused in Cyrillic WoD community firsthand.<br /> Even the original idea sounds better than what we got in the end. Not sure what forced authors to go that other way which inevitably leads to tasteless stuff like &quot;Stalin was a Baali!&quot;. <br /> <br /> If nothing, things like these are why we can't have the nice ones and why exploring more complex and controversial themes than crying over your dead friend or waging turf wars a-la san andreas became way more difficult, in times of the court of public opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:00:07-07:00","id":1379975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malkav19</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra#post1379759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> <br /> &quot;thinking the ashirra is a single thing, a single culture, is a prejudiced idea that will get you killed in the courts of the future. consider this: among our new allies we find saudi princes dining on the blood of women stoned to death for infidelity, a liberal \u0131t-millionnaire from jordan, turkish nationalists dreaming of the ottoman empire, kurdish freedom fighters and persian nobles longing for the glorious days of disco in 1970\u2019s teheran. they are all ashirra. they all believe in allah\u2019s pillars. yet none of them think and act in the same way.&quot;<br /> </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with an in-world character having a specific worldview which bleeds through into their comments on in-world topics. My litmus test for whether a passage is well done is whether it is internally consistent for the speaker's world-view.<br /> <br /> And it is...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> thinking the ashirra is a single thing, a single culture, is a prejudiced idea that will get you killed in the courts of the future. </div> </div> </div>The speaker clearly believes in a multi-cultural, citizen of the world ethos. Other in-world characters may or may not agree; indeed, the fact that the speaker emphasizes multiculturalism, and warns that parochialism will get one killed, implies some in-world characters are not so cosmopolitan. In real life, you or I might agree with one side or the other... or neither... but the passage is meant to tell us something of the tensions that exist for in-world characters. It has not been easy for Eurocentric Camarilla to adjust to a wider world of vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> among our new allies </div> </div> </div>Not &quot;among the Ashirra&quot;, or &quot;among the A-Rabs&quot;, or even &quot;within the Umma&quot;... all of which would have communicated a different world-view... but &quot;new allies&quot;. The speaker is not afraid to stake out a position, while almost daring the listener to contradict the implicit assumptions that are signaled. Classic Brujah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> we find saudi princes dining on the blood of women stoned to death for infidelity </div> </div> </div>This passage is interesting, because there are several coded statements in it. The most obvious is &quot;those wacky Saudis, with their morality laws&quot;... a view which has become more complex and more nuanced just since the book was published.<br /> <br /> There is a subtler dig at the Saudi vampiric leaders, though. Read more carefully, the speaker is saying that Saudi vampires have princes so weak-blooded they can partake in the revolting practice of drinking the blood of mutilated corpses. Mechanically, this would require the Iron Gullet advantage, and likely a blood potency of 2 or lower. There is a pile of generational-classism in this insult, with its dismissal of Saudi princes as simultaneously nouveau riche and barbaric.<br /> <br /> Never mind that it seems <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capital_punishment_in_Saudi_Arabia#Adultery\" target=\"_blank\">unlikely</a> someone could make such feeding a staple of their diet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a liberal \u0131t-millionnaire from jordan </div> </div> </div>Think about the subtleties of how this line could have been structured, and how different the implied meaning is in each:<br /> &quot;a Jordanian it-millionaire, who is liberal&quot;<br /> &quot;a liberal Jordanian it-techie, who is a millionaire&quot;<br /> &quot;a Jordanian liberal millionaire, who made their money in IT&quot;<br /> <br /> In the original, the traits &quot;liberal&quot;, &quot;IT&quot;, and &quot;millionaire&quot; are all run together, as if they are self-reinforcing rather than contradictory traits. Splitting those traits with a conjunction from the remaining trait &quot;Jordan(ian)&quot;, implies there is some surprise to be had with somebody from Jordan running a tech startup. The speaker is trying soooo hard to be inclusive, and stumbles into the false stereotype of Arabs living in technologically backward countries. (<a href=\"http://amcham.jo/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/IB-Jordans-IT-Sector.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">PDF: Jordan is quite tech forward</a>.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> turkish nationalists dreaming of the ottoman empire, </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing the speaker sees this as a series of insults. &quot;Nationalists!&quot; &quot;Imperialists!&quot; &quot;Dreamers!&quot; As written, there is an implicit warning that this is a movement that must be monitored, especially since the speaker is alternating in a bad-good-bad-good pattern in their list. There could have been a more neutral description like, &quot;Turkish vampires who hope to advance the fortunes of their country, using the Ottoman Empire as inspiration&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> kurdish freedom fighters and persian nobles longing for the glorious days of disco in 1970\u2019s teheran </div> </div> </div>True, the passage could have been written with &quot;terrorist&quot; or &quot;nationalist militiamen&quot; in place of &quot;freedom fighters&quot;. Then again, &quot;glorious&quot; could have been replaced with &quot;decadent&quot; or even &quot;cheesy&quot;. None of these substitutions would have been consistent with the world-view portrayed in previous parts of the text, though.<br /> <br /> As written, there is an internal consistency to the passage. Same worldview, same prejudices, same tone, even similar vocabulary. As is usual with a fictional character's statement of opinion we learn as much about the speaker as about the topic they are discussing.<br /> <br /> I kind of think it's cool that Kurdish freedom fighters and Persian nobles both share nostalgia for the glory days of disco. Even freedom fighters need to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5ObWgbBlcj4\" target=\"_blank\">boogie down</a> once in a while.<br /> <br /> Or, was there an <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serial_comma\" target=\"_blank\">Oxford comma</a> in the original text?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T20:27:00-07:00","id":1380012,"title":"","content":"I think the comma is implied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T08:08:13-07:00","id":1380121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1379816#post1379816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few random factoids for the complicated political and economic elements of a RL matter in the World of Darkness:<br /> <br /> 1. The United States actually re-allied with the Kurds almost immediately after abandoning them and they remain the US' allies.<br /> <br /> 2. The Kurdish resistance in Syria are listed as a terrorist organization primarily by Russia, Assad, and Turkey due to the fact that they are interested in establishing a Kurdish state.<br /> <br /> 3. The Kurds have been allies of the USA since the US took over administration of Iraq-Kurd territory when chemical weapons were used against them.<br /> <br /> 4. It's a talking point that the Afghanistan freedom fighters against the Soviet Union (which they were) became the Taliban. The issue is a bit more complicated than that and could better be summarized as, &quot;The resistance against the Soviet Union succeeded but was then replaced by a reactionary Islamic fundamentalist state founded by their own children, many of which were raised by clerics they'd been kept with during the war. Those who resisted were killed.&quot;<br /> <br /> 5. The treatment of the Kurds as terrorists is kind of an international joke that ****ing Call of Duty made fun of as insane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/XCKsZGVIlUw\" data-code=\"XCKsZGVIlUw\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XCKsZGVIlUw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> 6. Al-Qaeda or &quot;The Foundation&quot; was founded by a Saudi Arabian group trying to get Americans out of Saudi Arabia that became a more generic anti-American one. It was given host by the Taliban and carried out attacks on the US from their soil prior to 9/11. Hence why it was justified under international law to invade them given they were receiving sanctuary and support by the Taliban.<br /> <br /> 7. This is a good argument why all commentary should be done in-universe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are really lots of factoids here, so let me switch back to the facts:<br /> <br /> 1-They may remain as US allies but that doesn't change a shit: A couple of years ago senator Lindsey Graham was arguing that the US has created a mess in the Turkish border by supporting the YPG (see: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-y41XeGLTjI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-y41XeGLTjI</a>).<br /> <br /> 2-Russia doesn't list them as terrorists, on the contrary, they opened an office in Moscow (see: <a href=\"https://www.rt.com/news/332077-kurdish-representative-office-moscow/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.rt.com/news/332077-kurdi...office-moscow/</a>). Assad's stance on them can never be thought independent of Russia's stance as he owes Russian's big time. Turkey lists them terrorists because YPG shares an intellectual lineage and certain overlaps in memberships and militant recruitments with the PKK (see: <a href=\"https://foreignpolicy.com/2019/10/17/turkey-claim-syrian-kurds-terrorists-not-isis-ypg-pkk-sdf/\" target=\"_blank\">https://foreignpolicy.com/2019/10/17...s-ypg-pkk-sdf/</a>),<br /> <br /> 3- Iraqi Kurdistan is not led by PKK/YPG, it's under the KDP rule (Barzanis).<br /> <br /> 4- As you can see from what you say yourself, terms like terrorist and freedom fighter are not neutral.<br /> <br /> 5- It's not a joke, it is totally normal. If you kill civilians (<a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/article/us-syria-security-blast/turkey-says-two-killed-in-car-bomb-attack-near-syria-border-idUSKBN20A0KD\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.reuters.com/article/us-s...-idUSKBN20A0KD</a>), displace people (<a href=\"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2015/10/syria-us-allys-razing-of-villages-amounts-to-war-crimes/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/ne...to-war-crimes/</a>), recruit the children (<a href=\"https://www.hrw.org/news/2018/08/03/syria-armed-group-recruiting-children-camps\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.hrw.org/news/2018/08/03/...children-camps</a>) for your cause, eventually, somebody will call you a terrorist.<br /> <br /> Just imagine that Albertzen was calling ISIS freedom fighters. If you are ok with this, then you're consistent when you're ok with the term Kurdish freedom fighters (again I think the YPG was implied here). And personally, it\u2019d be a lot more provocative (in a good way) as it\u2019s something different than just repeating the Western mainstream media rhetoric (i.e. the YPG is a bunch of freedom fighters).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1379975#post1379975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> True, the passage could have been written with &quot;terrorist&quot; or &quot;nationalist militiamen&quot; in place of &quot;freedom fighters&quot;. Then again, &quot;glorious&quot; could have been replaced with &quot;decadent&quot; or even &quot;cheesy&quot;. None of these substitutions would have been consistent with the world-view portrayed in previous parts of the text, though.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The term 'freedom fighters' and the adjective 'glorious' are not very comparable if you ask me. While the former involves killing people, the latter only describes some nostalgia.<br /> <br /> edit: But in overall, I'm kind of convinced that a Cam brujah could call them freedom fighters, why not? And to be honest, i was just me who took them as the YPG, they might be anyone basically as there are many different Kurdish groups that are already mentioned within this discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26081-malkav19","user":"malkav19","date":". 04-10-2020, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26081-malkav19","name":"malkav19","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T11:17:05-07:00","id":1380161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malkav19</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1380121#post1380121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The term 'freedom fighters' and the adjective 'glorious' are not very comparable if you ask me. While the former involves killing people, the latter only describes some nostalgia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was discussing writing, grammar, and syntax, so they are <i>quite</i> compara...<br /> <br /> Oh.<br /> <br /> Wait.<br /> <br /> I understand now.<br /> <br /> You have no interest whatsoever in whether the passage you quoted is an effective piece of writing used to show readers what a fictional character in a fictional world believes about that fictional world. You just want to assume that everything that comes out of every character's mouth represents the heartfelt beliefs of the writer... I assume so you can then feel superior to the writer by &quot;correcting&quot; them.<br /> <br /> You seem to have so little interest in the actual content and context of the phrasing, you don't even bother to quote it accurately... or was it originally published in all lower case letters, with haphazard punctuation? (In fairness, punctuation and copy editing is not V5's strong suit, so maybe fair play.)<br /> <br /> If you feel like taking a faux-profound stance against the very phrase &quot;freedom fighters&quot;, perhaps it would prove helpful to the writers of the world if you provided a list of phrases you feel must never be used again, even in the process of showing what a fictional character in a fictional world believes about that fictional world.<br /> <br /> I'll start with a list of phrases and words I wish were banned, under penalty of criminal law:<ul><li>I would ban &quot;passed away&quot; to indicate death. There is no physical movement involved.</li> <li>&quot;Artisanal&quot; is just a way of saying the maker lacks the cash to buy modern equipment. I hereby ban it.</li> <li>&quot;Hereby&quot; is pretentious and unnecessary outside the unique context of a legal document.</li> <li>&quot;Unique&quot; in any situation where it is not true, which is literally every time it is used.</li> <li>&quot;Literally&quot;, which is uniquely similar to the above word.</li> <li>&quot;Firstly&quot;. Adverbs are totally unnecessary in mostly every situation.</li> <li>&quot;Thusly&quot;, except when used by uneducated people trying to sound educated. We can't help it.</li> <li>&quot;Vayjayjay&quot; and &quot;peepee&quot;. Unless the speaker is three and still learning to speak, in which case the word shouldn't be used at all outside of a medical or hygiene context.</li> <li>&quot;Saga&quot;, except when used to describe stories from Old Norse, or comparing something to those. ex: &quot;The story of how you got a flat tire on your way to work is not a saga.&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Enervate&quot;, &quot;Irony&quot;, and &quot;Nauseous&quot;. They don't mean what you think they mean.</li> <li>&quot;Awesome&quot;. Okay, fine, use it for a tornado you can see heading your way, but not for the nachos you ate while high.</li> </ul><br /> Which other words and phrases would you like to put on the no-no list? I'll promise to no longer use them, if you agree to avoid the terms I listed. F---dom fi---er will evermore spring from my mouth as &quot;the eff-eff word&quot;.<br /> <br /> Before you do, though, I'd like to share one of my other pet peeves. In the Christian Bible (John 20:25, kjv), the Apostle Thomas says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ..he said unto them, Except I shall see in his hands the print of the nails, and put my finger into the print of the nails, and thrust my hand into his side, I will not believe. </div> </div> </div>It has always bothered me that John doesn't believe in the resurrection. I mean, really, he was a writer of a gospel! If he showed a character talking like that, clearly John himself felt that way. Everything character portrayed by a writer is just a mouthpiece for the writer's views, and no character would ever say any little phrase that doesn't conform to the writer's views. So, John must have been a skeptic!<br /> <br /> Because, that's how writing works, right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T12:05:15-07:00","id":1380169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1380161#post1380161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I was discussing writing, grammar, and syntax, so they are <i>quite</i> compara...<br /> <br /> Oh.<br /> <br /> Wait.<br /> <br /> I understand now.<br /> <br /> You have no interest whatsoever in whether the passage you quoted is an effective piece of writing used to show readers what a fictional character in a fictional world believes about that fictional world. You just want to assume that everything that comes out of every character's mouth represents the heartfelt beliefs of the writer... I assume so you can then feel superior to the writer by &quot;correcting&quot; them.<br /> <br /> You seem to have so little interest in the actual content and context of the phrasing, you don't even bother to quote it accurately... or was it originally published in all lower case letters, with haphazard punctuation? (In fairness, punctuation and copy editing is not V5's strong suit, so maybe fair play.)<br /> <br /> If you feel like taking a faux-profound stance against the very phrase &quot;freedom fighters&quot;, perhaps it would prove helpful to the writers of the world if you provided a list of phrases you feel must never be used again, even in the process of showing what a fictional character in a fictional world believes about that fictional world.<br /> <br /> I'll start with a list of phrases and words I wish were banned, under penalty of criminal law:<ul><li>I would ban &quot;passed away&quot; to indicate death. There is no physical movement involved.</li> <li>&quot;Artisanal&quot; is just a way of saying the maker lacks the cash to buy modern equipment. I hereby ban it.</li> <li>&quot;Hereby&quot; is pretentious and unnecessary outside the unique context of a legal document.</li> <li>&quot;Unique&quot; in any situation where it is not true, which is literally every time it is used.</li> <li>&quot;Literally&quot;, which is uniquely similar to the above word.</li> <li>&quot;Firstly&quot;. Adverbs are totally unnecessary in mostly every situation.</li> <li>&quot;Thusly&quot;, except when used by uneducated people trying to sound educated. We can't help it.</li> <li>&quot;Vayjayjay&quot; and &quot;peepee&quot;. Unless the speaker is three and still learning to speak, in which case the word shouldn't be used at all outside of a medical or hygiene context.</li> <li>&quot;Saga&quot;, except when used to describe stories from Old Norse, or comparing something to those. ex: &quot;The story of how you got a flat tire on your way to work is not a saga.&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Enervate&quot;, &quot;Irony&quot;, and &quot;Nauseous&quot;. They don't mean what you think they mean.</li> <li>&quot;Awesome&quot;. Okay, fine, use it for a tornado you can see heading your way, but not for the nachos you ate while high.</li> </ul><br /> Which other words and phrases would you like to put on the no-no list? I'll promise to no longer use them, if you agree to avoid the terms I listed. F---dom fi---er will evermore spring from my mouth as &quot;the eff-eff word&quot;.<br /> <br /> Before you do, though, I'd like to share one of my other pet peeves. In the Christian Bible (John 20:25, kjv), the Apostle Thomas says:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It has always bothered me that John doesn't believe in the resurrection. I mean, really, he was a writer of a gospel! If he showed a character talking like that, clearly John himself felt that way. Everything character portrayed by a writer is just a mouthpiece for the writer's views, and no character would ever say any little phrase that doesn't conform to the writer's views. So, John must have been a skeptic!<br /> <br /> Because, that's how writing works, right?</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You are right about that I didn't quote it accurately: I sent it to a friend on a different website which doesn't let you use upper case letters and then, I directly copied from there when I was writing my first message. Believe it or not. But it doesn't mean that I have little interest in the actual content.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Another thing that you are right, is your assumptions about my take on the beliefs of the writer. I shouldn't have done that (I'm serious!).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But one thing you should understand is not everything inside the book is fictional: Syrian civil war, president Assad, Taliban and so on. These are real issues with some serious real consequences for people who you'll probably never have a chance to meet. As I said many times, the widespread rhetoric in the Western media is that the YPG is a bunch of freedom fighters, and with the timing of the release of the book, I've speculated that they were being implied and I've just voiced my personal opinion and counterargument. As I said it'd be a lot better for me to see ISIS freedom fighters (as it'd be way more provocative and horrific in a good way) or more neutral terms. But it's just me, and I'm feeling like I was wrong to make assumptions/speculations in the first place. So chill, I don't have any no-no list or whatsoever. Glad that I've managed to amuse you though!</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26081-malkav19","name":"malkav19","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T12:43:52-07:00","id":1380181,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26081-malkav19\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26081\" data-vbnamecard=\"26081\">malkav19</a> <br /> <br /> You're right that not every element in the book is fictional. This is inevitable in a fictional world based closely on the real world, and I think we can agree that the writers of the V5 line have not always navigated this very well.<br /> <br /> One thing I'd like to see in game publishing is more products written by people with direct experience of the regions they describe. For example, I'd love to see an India by Night book, but would be rather nervous about it weren't primarily written by people from India.<br /> <br /> You have a good way with writing in your posts. Have you written any fan works, like Storyteller Vault products or fanfic, with characters close to your pov? I'm betting it would be a good read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T06:19:22-07:00","id":1380370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malkav19</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1380169#post1380169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">...But one thing you should understand is not everything inside the book is fictional: Syrian civil war...</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Book or no book, the &quot;Syrian civil war&quot; is, actually, fictional. It's odd that you keep mentioning &quot;western rhetoric&quot; when it's about the Kurds and yet you accept and use western rhetoric for the Syrian invasion/proxy war.<br /> <br /> If anything, it's more sound to call the Kurds as &quot;freedom fighters&quot; since, you said it yourself, it's &quot;a<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> relativistic term&quot; (at least at some level) than to call what happens in Syria as a &quot;civil war&quot;.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26036-smokewins","name":"SmokeWins","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T03:16:45-07:00","id":1380892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1380161#post1380161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll start with a list of phrases and words I wish were banned, under penalty of criminal law:<br /> {snip}<br /> Because, that's how writing works, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>A recent Economist article entitled &quot;Silly Sausages: Europe heroically defends itself against Veggie burgers&quot;..<br /> <br /> <i>The European Union gets a lot of flak. All right, it isn\u2019t literally blasted with anti-aircraft fire, but you know what we mean. One ongoing battle (OK, nobody died) involves the use of words. Earlier this year, the European Parliament\u2019s agriculture committee voted to prohibit the terms \u201cburger\u201d, \u201csausage\u201d, \u201cescalope\u201d and \u201csteak\u201d to describe products that do not contain any meat. It was inspired by the European Court of Justice\u2019s decision in 2017 to ban the use of \u201cmilk\u201d, \u201cbutter\u201d and \u201ccream\u201d for non-dairy products. Exceptions were made for \u201cice cream\u201d and \u201calmond milk\u201d, but \u201csoya milk\u201d went down the drain, lest consumers assume it had been extracted from the soya udder of a soya cow. The court has yet to rule on the milk of human kindness.<br /> <br /> Greens are mounting a campaign against the committee\u2019s decision, which they suspect is supported not only by linguistic purists but also by the meat industry. This newspaper thinks the parliament is quite right to protect citizens from the confusion they would no doubt feel were they to find that no part of a \u201cveggie burger\u201d was made of the flesh of a dead animal. Indeed, this praiseworthy initiative needs to go further.<br /> <br /> \u201cEscalopes\u201d pose a clear danger to consumers, who might well recoil in horror when, taking a mouthful of one, they discover that it is made not of the scallops from which it got its name but of chicken or veal. \u201cSausages\u201d should refer only to heavily salted meat, whence the term derives; for clarity, consumers should be informed that the item is encased in animal intestine. Steaks should be sold only on a pointed stick, on the grounds that most shoppers will rely on the proto-Indo-European etymology. Any confusion could be avoided if kebabs were, as their Arabic root suggests, always sold burned. The production of burgers should be restricted to the butchers of Hamburg, long ago deprived of their intellectual property by a shocking failure of linguistic regulation. The same right should be extended to makers of Frankfurter sausages\u2014sorry, meat-filled gut. And \u201cmeat\u201d itself should apply to all food, sweet or savoury, which would make the term historically accurate, if useless.<br /> <br /> Nor should the parliament\u2019s reforming zeal be restricted to food. Any reference to the European budget should be confined to the money that the commissioner for economic and monetary affairs, Valdis Dombrovskis, keeps on his person in a bougette, or leather purse. Only those banks which carry out their business on wooden benches (banco, in Italian) should be included in the banking union. Discussion of computers should be limited to clerks who do budgetary calculations, while that of the digital single market should apply only to sums that people can do on their fingers.<br /> <br /> This linguistic rigour should be extended through both time and space. The Holy Roman Empire, as Voltaire pointed out, was neither holy, nor Roman, nor an empire; La Manche has no sartorial connections; the Mediterranean is not the centre of the Earth; there is no horticulture in the Big Apple. They need renaming.<br /> <br /> Not all the union\u2019s governing structures are taking their linguistic responsibilities seriously enough. When earlier this year Donald Tusk, president of the European Council, spoke of \u201cconcrete measures\u201d to extend the single market and a \u201clevel playing field\u201d, listeners might reasonably have looked forward to a multi-billion-euro infrastructure project to shift French and Italian mountaintops to the low-lying bits around Brussels.<br /> <br /> The Treaty of Rome speaks of the need to respect member states\u2019 culture (no, nothing to do with yogurt) and bind them together (please put the string away). In view of those aspirations, Europe\u2019s leaders need to get on board with this reform. Not literally, obviously. It\u2019s not a ship. Never mind.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T04:01:20-07:00","id":1380897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malkav19</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1380169#post1380169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But one thing you should understand is not everything inside the book is fictional: </span></div> </div> </div> </div>It is in a way. There's <i>an </i>Assad in the World of Darkness, but it's not the <i>actual </i>Assad; it's a fictional analogue existing in an alternate reality.<br /> <br /> Using real-life events with real-life mass casualties as a backdrop for an entertainment medium is always going to have a problematic aspect. One can't avoid it entirely without turning the World of Darkness into the World of Candyfloss, and the bounds of acceptability are as much a matter of gut instinct as logic. For me it's partly about how many grieving relatives are still out there. I would recoil from using 9/11 (casualties c. 3,000) as part of a plot in a way that I probably wouldn't about the London Blitz (casualties c. 28,000). I see the logic of the Beckoning drawing elders to the middle east (region in turmoil hides their activities, plus it's the site of some of the earliest human civilisations and so a likely spot for the eldest vampires to have gone to ground), but it still makes me a bit uneasy.<br /> <br /> So I remind myself that this is one of what GURPS would call the Infinite Worlds, and everything that happens there <b><i>is </i></b>fictional, even if it follows the pattern of events in reality","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T04:37:47-07:00","id":1380907,"title":"","content":"One might argue this is a good reason for why you might use fictional analogs to real life characters.<br /> <br /> In my Agent G books, which are a cyberpunk series set in present days, I had &quot;Karl Trust&quot; as the President. He's got some stereotypical and overtly ridiculous Right Wing cariacture elements but he's not trying to assign them to any real politicians.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T01:47:14-07:00","id":1381244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1379854#post1379854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, right, sensitive territories and all, complex topic and that, but let's bring this down to vampires<br /> <br /> From Any vampires point of view, is what the OP's quoted actually appropriate? Consider this; The Ashirra doesn't cover one city that covers the entire middle east, it's in <i>different</i> cities. The Saud and the turk are going to be far, far away from eachother, just like there are few Germans in france.<br /> From an Elders perspective; Do they really care about the many, many mortal groups that are taking up arms for various ideologies? A lot of these groups have only popped up in the last century or so. It isn't just elders, it's Ancillae that predate the borders and factions of the land.<br /> <br /> To me it just reads like someone wanting to appear culturally sensitive, without actually considering that much.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, it does matter, because they are actually making the same point you just made. Thinking of the Ashirra being the same everywhere will get you dead, oh and we see from previous editions and the DA line that, yes, Vampires care, especially those on Humanity, about mortal conflicts and ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T03:39:40-07:00","id":1381254,"title":"","content":"But how does that actually translate into practice? <br /> <br /> A vampire walks around Bagdad and someone a someone points out &quot;IT WOULD BE A MISTAKE TO THINK THIS IS ISTAMBUL. as if, y'know, I could only tell the differences between London and Vilnius because... erm... Europeans have more variety in hair colour or something? It just reads like pretentious, condesending nonsense brought about by an inferiority complex. Fuck, Vampire gives us a setting where Chicago is a completely different city to Gary, and yet this author wants to make a big deal out of how diverse the middle east is. It's just undeserved. <br /> <br /> As for Vampires. <br /> Yeah, sure, they'll meddle. <br /> But if you look at the history of the middle east, the events that turned it into the quagmire it is today started after first world war; The ottomans lost their influence, France and Britain played colonialism, the Saudis took power, religious fires got stoked up, Some revolutions occured, some counter revolutions occured... <br /> This all happened just a little more than a hundred years ago. While neonates get rilled up by the recent politics of their breathing days, those with power, ancillae and elders, are older than this. Most in power would hail from the rule of the Ottoman Empire or Persia. They may play sides with modern newfangled modern extremists, but that's for their own agendas. <br /> <br /> You don't need someone to tell you that Istambul is not Baghdad. My problem here is that the Author seems to really, really wants some kind of... Multiculturalism without any blending, which is ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T06:38:54-07:00","id":1381631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmokeWins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1380370#post1380370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Book or no book, the &quot;Syrian civil war&quot; is, actually, fictional. It's odd that you keep mentioning &quot;western rhetoric&quot; when it's about the Kurds and yet you accept and use western rhetoric for the Syrian invasion/proxy war.<br /> <br /> If anything, it's more sound to call the Kurds as &quot;freedom fighters&quot; since, you said it yourself, it's &quot;a<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> relativistic term&quot; (at least at some level) than to call what happens in Syria as a &quot;civil war&quot;.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, I did the same mistake that I was criticizing. In the book, however, Hassan Shadid, a young Cam member from Iraq also uses the same definition for the proxy war. Maybe there could have been a touch on that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1381254#post1381254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how does that actually translate into practice?<br /> <br /> You don't need someone to tell you that Istambul is not Baghdad. My problem here is that the Author seems to really, really wants some kind of... Multiculturalism without any blending, which is ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>This also seems convincing! But not Istambul, Istanbul :P<br /> Also, one friend of mine reminded me that even Turkey used its own Kurdish \u201cfreedom fighters\u201d against the YPG in Syria (see: <a href=\"https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/turkey-sends-kurdish-falcon-force-afrin-counter-anti-kurd-image\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/t...nti-kurd-image</a>). So, I was totally wrong in the first place to think that Albertzen (or writer) was implying the YPG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1380181#post1380181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26081-malkav19\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26081\" data-vbnamecard=\"26081\">malkav19</a><br /> <br /> You're right that not every element in the book is fictional. This is inevitable in a fictional world based closely on the real world, and I think we can agree that the writers of the V5 line have not always navigated this very well.<br /> <br /> One thing I'd like to see in game publishing is more products written by people with direct experience of the regions they describe. For example, I'd love to see an India by Night book, but would be rather nervous about it weren't primarily written by people from India.<br /> <br /> You have a good way with writing in your posts. Have you written any fan works, like Storyteller Vault products or fanfic, with characters close to your pov? I'm betting it would be a good read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, but not yet! And yes, I totally agree about what you say about the direct experience from the regions and navigation in general.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26081-malkav19","name":"malkav19","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:16:47-07:00","id":1381686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malkav19</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379759-kurdish-freedom-fighters-in-ashirra?p=1381631#post1381631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right, I did the same mistake that I was criticizing. In the book, however, Hassan Shadid, a young Cam member from Iraq also uses the same definition for the proxy war. Maybe there could have been a touch on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I won't hold my breath for a change on that. It's just a game after all so, hopefully, people won't rely on it to learn but to just be entertained. [j/k]Plus...what do you expect from a Cammie?? :q[/jk]<br /> <br /> Even history books &amp; historians have to be thoroughly checked (especially nowdays IMHO). Anyone with a piece of paper (diplomas etc which unfortunatelly get instant, undeserved, respect) can write and publish whatever nonsense feels like either for profit or for an agenda and many readers have no idea.<br /> <br /> Anyway, nice talking to you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26036-smokewins","name":"SmokeWins","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}